  "description": "Manurewa covers the southern Auckland suburbs of Manukau Central, Wiri, and Weymouth. The seat is held by Labour’s Arena Williams, who was first elected in 2020 and won re-election in 2023 with a margin of 16,261. Labour also won the party vote with 52% of the vote, followed by National with 29%. The electorate has only ever returned one list MP - National’s Cam Calder between 2009 and 2014.\n\n",
